Actually, the API timestamp corresponds to the current time when the request was made (it returns the position "now"). So ts ≈ now at fetch time. So p = (now - ts_ms)/POLL_MS with clamp01 works and is simpler. But using the sample's ts for ground speed: dt = (ts_new - ts_old). Good.

